  "body": "### Summary\nGenerate, on the Mac, legacy-app samples of the five on-device formats that LOT-067 (#92) must import, so that the importer is tested against what the legacy app really writes, never against hand-built plists (LESSONS 35-36).\n\n### Scope\nRun the legacy app (hfrnow @ `2440d79`, with the oracle tooling of `tooling/legacy-oracle/`, as for `samples/storage-smileys.json`, LOT-004) on **synthetic data** and export, for each format, the bytes the legacy app stores:\n\n| # | Legacy store | Where legacy keeps it | Legacy source |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `SuperFavoritesIds` | `UserDefaults` array | `Favorites.swift:114-136` |\n| 2 | `CollapsedFavoriteSectionIDs` | `UserDefaults` array | `Favorites.swift` (`FavoritesCollapsedSectionsStore`) |\n| 3 | `smiley_favorites_cache2` | `NSKeyedArchiver` file | `SmileyCache.m:18-35, 353-439` |\n| 4 | `smileySearchHistory_v1` | JSON file | `SmileySearchService.swift:85-125` |\n| 5 | `rehostImagesSwiftUI.json` | JSON file | `ReplyService.swift:1898-1911` |\n\nFor each: at least an empty, a typical and a boundary sample, for example:\n- super-favourites: the same topic number in two categories;\n- search history: exactly 50 entries;\n- upload history: one corrupt file, since legacy rewrites it as empty.\n\nAdd the `UserDefaults` domain dump (`defaults export`) holding #1 and #2.\n\n### Rules\n- **Synthetic data only.** No real pseudo, no real topic of a member, no cookie or token. Anonymize per `docs/FIXTURES.md`; an independent reviewer checks the samples before the push (LESSONS 33-34).\n- The legacy app is **not** patched beyond the oracle patch of the branch (`run-oracle.sh` refuses otherwise).\n- One PR with the samples under `tooling/legacy-oracle/samples/` plus their MANIFEST rows.\n\n### Wanted by\n- LOT-067 (#92), legacy data import on update. Every lot it depends on is done (LOT-064 merged in #345). This capture is its only blocker.\n- Then LOT-158 (#248), the first-launch import (M4).\n\n### Source\nLOT-064 spec (`docs/lots/LOT-064-small-stores.md`, \"Fixtures\" and \"Pending capture\"), merged in #345.",
